        "approximationNote": "VERY LOW CONFIDENCE representative former-estate-adjacent rural landscape tract, not a recovered historic compound or estate perimeter. Primary municipal text says the hamlet disappeared; archival name records confirm its identity and place it north of Babosdöbréte. The historical name point falls in this coherent rural tract north of the current village core. Seven native tracks supply most exterior edges, the actual Babosdöbréte administrative boundary supplies 998 m of necessary closure, and a native forest ring is an interior exclusion. No invented edge, circle, radius, point-only polygon, hull, snapping or viewport perimeter is used. No other known place label or native residential/farmyard/industrial surface is inside. No extracted building intersects; the 1.5 km building-extraction window covers 95.93% of the tract and makes no completeness claim for its northern tip. Historic ownership, parcel extent and former six-house compound location are not recovered. This partial landscape representation is only a rough locality estimate and makes no current occupancy or cadastral accuracy claim. Municipal PDF map pixels were not seen or digitized; the geometry comes solely from archived native source edges.",
